        "example": "The AFTER trigger logs after the update succeeds. The INSTEAD OF trigger intercepts DELETE and raises an error instead, completely preventing the deletion.",
        "code": "-- AFTER Trigger: Log after successful update\nCREATE TRIGGER trg_LogUpdate ON Employees AFTER UPDATE AS\nBEGIN INSERT INTO AuditLog(TableChanged, Action, ChangeDate) VALUES ('Employees', 'UPDATE', GETDATE()); END;\n-- INSTEAD OF Trigger: Prevent delete with reason\nCREATE TRIGGER trg_PreventDelete ON Employees INSTEAD OF DELETE AS\nBEGIN RAISERROR('Employee deletion is not allowed. Use soft delete instead.', 16, 1); END;",
