        "explanation": "Common aggregate functions include COUNT() (count rows), SUM() (total values), AVG() (average), MAX() (largest value), MIN() (smallest value), COUNT(DISTINCT) (count unique values), STDEV() (standard deviation), and VAR() (variance). They operate on sets of rows and return a single value.\\n\\nAggregate functions operate on sets of rows and return a single value. Common ones include COUNT() for row counting, SUM() for totals, AVG() for averages, MAX() for largest values, and MIN() for smallest values. COUNT(*) counts all rows including NULLs; COUNT(column) excludes NULLs; COUNT(DISTINCT column) counts unique non-NULL values. All aggregates except COUNT(*) ignore NULL values.",
